1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,478
Last time the crew went into a ruin.

2
00:00:04,378 --> 00:00:06,987
Today there's no ruin at all.

3
00:00:08,787 --> 00:00:12,265
It's the same suit, and the same tools,

4
00:00:12,715 --> 00:00:15,759
outside a station, on a repair job.

5
00:00:16,659 --> 00:00:20,137
A crew member comes out of the airlock,

6
00:00:20,587 --> 00:00:24,065
flies round the hull, and welds a mast.

7
00:00:25,865 --> 00:00:29,778
And it's one more record than you already know.

8
00:00:30,978 --> 00:00:38,370
A crew member can go outside wherever the game has a space to fly a suit in.

9
00:00:39,270 --> 00:00:41,878
That's what a ruin's records are:

10
00:00:42,328 --> 00:00:45,807
rooms, a way in, and places to go.

11
00:00:47,607 --> 00:00:51,085
So a worksite is written as a ruin,

12
00:00:51,535 --> 00:00:55,448
with everything that looks like a ruin switched off.

13
00:00:56,348 --> 00:01:00,696
It has no walls, no drifting rock, and no cloud.

14
00:01:01,596 --> 00:01:03,770
One room to work in,

15
00:01:04,220 --> 00:01:07,698
and one solid lump where the station is.

16
00:01:09,498 --> 00:01:12,541
And there's one new record, the job.

17
00:01:13,441 --> 00:01:16,920
It's written like the barrier from last time,

18
00:01:17,370 --> 00:01:19,978
but it's never in anybody's way.

19
00:01:21,178 --> 00:01:22,917
Here are four records.

20
00:01:23,817 --> 00:01:26,426
The first is the worksite itself.

21
00:01:26,876 --> 00:01:32,528
It has no Relic line, so it's a second ruin, beside the Hollow.

22
00:01:33,428 --> 00:01:36,037
It sits at zero, zero, zero,

23
00:01:36,487 --> 00:01:39,965
which is where the template puts the station.

24
00:01:40,865 --> 00:01:43,909
It says walls, none, and debris, zero,

25
00:01:44,359 --> 00:01:46,967
and it has no Atmosphere line.

26
00:01:48,767 --> 00:01:53,115
Then one round room, fifteen hundred across from the middle.

27
00:01:54,015 --> 00:01:55,754
Then comes a solid,

28
00:01:56,204 --> 00:01:59,683
which takes the middle five hundred back out,

29
00:02:00,133 --> 00:02:04,915
so a suit flies round the station and not through it.

30
00:02:06,715 --> 00:02:08,454
And last the airlock.

31
00:02:09,354 --> 00:02:11,528
It wears the role entrance,

32
00:02:11,978 --> 00:02:14,587
so it's where the suit appears,

33
00:02:15,037 --> 00:02:18,080
and where suit up is measured from.

34
00:02:19,280 --> 00:02:22,759
The rule is the one from last time.

35
00:02:23,209 --> 00:02:27,991
The ship has to be within three thousand of the entrance.

36
00:02:29,791 --> 00:02:33,270
Now, a ship doesn't always start that close.

37
00:02:34,170 --> 00:02:38,083
In my two tests it started twenty-three hundred away,

38
00:02:38,533 --> 00:02:40,272
and then forty-three hundred.

39
00:02:41,172 --> 00:02:45,520
So if the app offers nothing, fly toward the station.

40
00:02:47,320 --> 00:02:50,363
And with two ruins in one mission,

41
00:02:50,813 --> 00:02:52,987
the offer follows the ship.

42
00:02:53,887 --> 00:02:58,235
It's the worksite here, and the Hollow at the Hollow.

43
00:02:59,435 --> 00:03:01,609
Now for the job itself.

44
00:03:02,509 --> 00:03:06,857
Repair, three numbers for where, and one for how big.

45
00:03:07,757 --> 00:03:12,539
I've put it just outside the hull, on the airlock's side.

46
00:03:14,339 --> 00:03:16,513
It says Clear with, beam,

47
00:03:16,963 --> 00:03:19,572
so the crew member welds it.

48
00:03:20,472 --> 00:03:23,950
The tools are the ones from last time:

49
00:03:24,400 --> 00:03:26,139
the beam, the tether,

50
00:03:26,589 --> 00:03:29,198
or a check of somebody's skill.

51
00:03:30,398 --> 00:03:34,746
When a job is done, the game sends a word.

52
00:03:35,646 --> 00:03:39,124
It's the job's key, and then underscore repaired.

53
00:03:40,024 --> 00:03:43,937
So my quest says done when, signal, mast repaired.

54
00:03:45,737 --> 00:03:50,085
That's three words now that the game sends by itself.

55
00:03:50,985 --> 00:03:52,724
A barrier has opened,

56
00:03:53,174 --> 00:03:55,348
a job has been repaired,

57
00:03:55,798 --> 00:03:58,841
or a ruin's piece has been taken.

58
00:03:59,741 --> 00:04:01,480
Lint knows all three.

59
00:04:02,680 --> 00:04:07,463
Now here's the reason I kept this in the same mission.

60
00:04:08,363 --> 00:04:11,841
I have two places with the role entrance.

61
00:04:12,291 --> 00:04:14,030
The game needs both.

62
00:04:15,830 --> 00:04:18,874
But my story uses that word too.

63
00:04:19,774 --> 00:04:23,252
The first step says reach entrance, one thousand.

64
00:04:24,152 --> 00:04:27,630
And reach doesn't know which entrance I meant.

65
00:04:29,430 --> 00:04:34,648
So a suit that steps out of the airlock at the station

66
00:04:35,098 --> 00:04:37,272
is standing on an entrance,

67
00:04:37,722 --> 00:04:39,896
and the step finishes there.

68
00:04:40,796 --> 00:04:45,143
It pays, and it sends the crew to the altar,

69
00:04:45,593 --> 00:04:47,333
before they've left home.

70
00:04:49,133 --> 00:04:50,872
Lint can't see it.

71
00:04:51,322 --> 00:04:53,061
Both lines are correct.

72
00:04:53,961 --> 00:04:57,439
The cure is a role of my own.

73
00:04:58,339 --> 00:05:01,817
I add hollow door to the Way In,

74
00:05:02,267 --> 00:05:04,876
and the step waits for that.

75
00:05:06,076 --> 00:05:09,554
Lint is clean, so I start the game.

76
00:05:10,454 --> 00:05:13,498
The Boarding Party app names the worksite,

77
00:05:13,948 --> 00:05:15,687
so I suit up.

78
00:05:17,487 --> 00:05:20,965
There's one place on the list, the mast.

79
00:05:21,415 --> 00:05:24,893
I pick it, and the suit flies round.

80
00:05:25,793 --> 00:05:29,272
On Fire, the row says Repair, Survey Mast.

81
00:05:30,172 --> 00:05:32,780
I select it, I press again,

82
00:05:33,230 --> 00:05:36,274
and the banner says repair, twelve seconds.

83
00:05:38,074 --> 00:05:39,813
And then it's done.

84
00:05:40,263 --> 00:05:44,611
The quest is finished, and I never sent the word.

85
00:05:45,811 --> 00:05:47,550
Now it's your turn.

86
00:05:48,450 --> 00:05:51,493
Add a valve that's worked by hand,

87
00:05:51,943 --> 00:05:54,987
and a panel that's hauled into place.

88
00:05:55,887 --> 00:05:58,930
Write a quest for one of them.

89
00:06:00,730 --> 00:06:04,643
Then break one line where lint can see it,

90
00:06:05,093 --> 00:06:07,267
and one where it can't.

91
00:06:08,167 --> 00:06:10,776
Next time is the last one:

92
00:06:11,226 --> 00:06:13,835
the whole class, in one episode.
